  "summary": "Universal curve fractal with infinite surface area and zero Lebesgue volume discovered by Karl Menger in 1926.",
  "description": "The Menger sponge is a 3D generalization of the Cantor set and Sierpi\u0144ski carpet, described by Austrian mathematician Karl Menger in 1926. It is constructed by repeatedly dividing each cube into  \\times 3 \\times 3 = 27$ sub-cubes and removing the central sub-cube and the 6 face-centered sub-cubes. Its Hausdorff dimension is $\\frac{\\ln 20}{\\ln 3} \\approx 2.7268$. Evaluated in Three.js using folded iterative domain distance estimation.",
